# Shell scripts and systemd units are consumed by Linux hosts and by
# go:embed, which embeds whatever bytes sit on disk at build time. A CRLF
# checkout on Windows would make the panel serve a script whose shebang ends
# in \r, and every node would die with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M". Pin
# them to LF on every platform regardless of core.autocrlf.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
